# Environment variables expected by the docker-compose templates in this dir.
# Copy to `.env` next to the compose file you want to use, fill in real values,
# then `docker compose -f docker-compose.<minimal|standard|full>.yml --env-file .env up -d`.
#
# The installer (install.sh / install.ps1) generates this file automatically
# when run in --mode docker. This template is for users who skip the
# installer and wire compose by hand.

# REQUIRED — long random string (≥32 bytes) used to sign dashboard cookies.
# Generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
DASHBOARD_SESSION_SECRET=

# OPTIONAL — at-rest AES key (≥32 bytes) for OAuth signing keys, service-
# connection secrets, git credentials, and plugin secrets. Independent of
# DASHBOARD_SESSION_SECRET above, so the session secret can be rotated
# without breaking encrypted data. Defaults to DASHBOARD_SESSION_SECRET when
# left unset. Never generate a fresh value here on an EXISTING installation —
# see the rotation runbook:
# docs/guides/security-administration.md#rotating-the-session-secret-and-the-at-rest-encryption-key
# DASHBOARD_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
